## Update a result

### Request attributes

Attribute           | Required | Description
--------------------|----------|------------
status              | Optional | Partner result status. If provided, it must be __"sending"__, __"sent"__, __"pending"__, __"completed"__ or __"failed"__.
summary             | Optional | Summary text shown on the candidate profile.
job-id              | Optional | ID of the job webhook was sent from.
url                 | Optional | URL for viewing a report on your website. Must be a valid HTTP or HTTPS URL.
label               | Optional | Free-form text naming the workflow that produced this result, shown in the candidate activity log. Maximum 255 characters. Updating it updates the activity log on next render. See [Label](#label).
assessment          | Optional | Assessment object. `score` must be between 0 and 100, `grade` may be __"top_fit"__, __"might_be_fit"__, __"might_not_be_fit"__, __"unknown"__ or __null__, and `duration` accepts seconds or `HH:MM:SS`.
details             | Optional | Details object displayed to the customer. Must be valid JSON with a maximum depth of 2.
attachments         | Optional | List of attachment objects containing exactly __"url"__ and __"description"__.
actions             | Optional | List of action objects containing `buttonText` and `endpoint`.
assessment-criteria | Optional | List of assessment criteria objects containing `id` and optional `score` between 0 and 100.
criteria            | Optional | Flat object of [moving criteria](#moving-criteria) values, keyed by the criterion `id`s you declared in your webhook config. Values are an outcome `id` or a number. Evaluated against the trigger's rules as soon as the update is saved.
candidate-id        | No       | __Immutable__. `candidate-id` is not updatable and should not be sent in update requests.

```http
PUT https://api.teamtailor.com/partner/v1/partner-results/3230d614-a33b-4a25-ac9c-4ec107e60f2e HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer abc123abc123
X-Api-Version: <%= config[:api_version] %>
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data":{
    "type": "partner-results",
    "id": "3230d614-a33b-4a25-ac9c-4ec107e60f2e",
    "attributes":{
      "status": "completed",
      "summary": "The candidate passed the test with excellent results",
      "label": "Backend Screening",
      "assessment": {
        "score": 82,
        "grade": "top_fit",
        "duration": "0:32:14"
      },
      "details": {
        "rating": "10",
        "awesomeness": "confirmed"
      },
      "criteria": {
        "report_decision": "clear",
        "risk_score": 2
      }
    }
  }
}
```
> Example response

```json
{
  "data": {
    "id": "3230d614-a33b-4a25-ac9c-4ec107e60f2e",
    "type": "partner-results",
    "links": {
      "self": "https://api.teamtailor.localhost/partner/v1/partner-results/3230d614-a33b-4a25-ac9c-4ec107e60f2e"
    },
    "attributes": {
      "assessment": {
        "score": 82,
        "grade": "top_fit",
        "duration": 1934
      },
      "details": {
        "rating": "10",
        "awesomeness": "confirmed"
      },
      "status": "completed",
      "summary": "The candidate passed the test with excellent results",
      "url": "http://www.example.com/test/1234",
      "label": "Backend Screening",
      "candidate-id": 102,
      "criteria": {
        "report_decision": "clear",
        "risk_score": 2
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Update a result by using the ID from the [Webhook object](#webhooks).

Updating a result is also what triggers stage routing. If the customer has built rules on your [moving criteria](#moving-criteria), Teamtailor evaluates them against the saved result immediately after the update, and moves the candidate when a rule matches.
